WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.273
Raw milk. Shaken, not stirred.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.107
Am I being detained? I'm filming you.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:12.933
I have a right to film
you. I'm in a public place.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:14.220
What is it?

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.833
Cutting edge nano technology.Smart blood.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.590
Microchips in your bloodstream

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.106
allows us to track your
movements in the field.

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.079
I've come to the wrong queue.

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:28.597
Gay wedding cake shaken, not stirred.

00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:32.010
Why does this bag of cocaine
have a CIA label on it?

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.900
Something we're making for the Americans,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.723
it's called a ghetto blaster.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.600
We definitely shouldn't do that.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.840
And we probably shouldn't call it that.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.200
Well, Mr. Bond,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.473
soon, the United States
debt will top $29 trillion.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.570
It's madness. Economic madness.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.200
How did you pull off this heinous act?

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.580
Oh, I had nothing to do with
it. No, it was Congress.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.150
Congress of the Soviet Union

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.390
tricked us into getting this debt.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.580
What? No, the United States Congress.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:01.500
Of America?.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.462
Yes.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.877
How much was it again?

00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:05.540
$29 trillion.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.373
Do we pay interest on that?

00:01:06.373 --> 00:01:07.470
Yes.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.303
All the time?

00:01:08.303 --> 00:01:09.136
Yes.

00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:09.969
This is terrifying.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.340
It's a great deal of money.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.173
What do we do?

00:01:12.173 --> 00:01:13.630
Honestly, it won't affect me very much

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.030
because I'm very wealthy.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:15.990
Will I be okay?

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.041
Are you a federal employee?

00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:17.874
Yes.

00:01:17.874 --> 00:01:18.707
Then you'll be fine.

00:01:18.707 --> 00:01:19.540
Oh, thank God.

00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:21.438
What a waste

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.550
of perfectly good gold.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.960
It's easily transferable. It's fungible.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.940
Not difficult to assay. The
hedge against inflation.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.750
It doesn't spoil. It's malleable.
We made it a microchip.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.230
Sold coins and gold jewelry

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.530
And then Nixon took us
off the gold standard.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.983
He's the true villain here.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.160
You know, you're quite a good listener.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:45.560
Usually people get bored
when I talk about gold.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.513
You all right?

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.680
Two fingers of LSD. Shaken, not stirred.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.440
Now pay attention, Bond.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.800
An ordinary pen. inside is
a fraction of a drop of ink.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.250
The rest is filled with a sense
of self-importance and the

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.450
desire to control the lives of others.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:09.200
My God, it would take 10 of
these just to sign your name.

00:02:14.229 --> 00:02:18.405
Ling, say goodbye to Felix. Man talk.

00:02:20.071 --> 00:02:21.450
I was a different person back then.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:25.060
I was literally a
different person back then.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.500
You carry a double O number.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.810
It means you're licensed
to kill, not get killed.

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.227
But I still need a license to braid hair?

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.390
Guess we're adding bagpipes to the list.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.560
I'll have a bacon wrapped
hotdog. Shaken, not stirred.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.513
I'll have a ginger ale and
Ayahuasca. Shaken, not stirred.

00:02:47.513 --> 00:02:48.793
One infant.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.053
Just hand it to me.

00:02:57.018 --> 00:03:00.435
Oh, so it's like, seasteading, only evil.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:02.630
Who are you?

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.033
My name is Pussy Galore.

00:03:06.061 --> 00:03:10.170
Oh, right. What are your pronouns?

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.900
Pay attention bond. An
ordinary household printer.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.480
However, if you press
this button right here,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.953
$1 trillion enters the money supply.

00:03:16.953 --> 00:03:18.410
Really? This button here?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.243
This button right here.

00:03:19.243 --> 00:03:20.076
Right there.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:23.940
No harm in it, right?

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.830
Well, Mr. Bond, it's time I leave you.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.630
I have a date with a rocket ship.

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.020
To blow up the moon?

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.520
Just to float about
for a bit as a tourist,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.849
it sounds really fun.

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:37.800
Using hard-earned taxpayer dollars?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.910
No I'm using my money.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.171
Money you stole.

00:03:41.171 --> 00:03:44.122
No. I provided goods and
services on the internet

00:03:44.122 --> 00:03:45.551
during a pandemic.

00:03:45.551 --> 00:03:48.278
I created a great amount
of value for many people

00:03:48.278 --> 00:03:49.523
all across the globe.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.030
I'm sorry, how is that evil?

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.908
I don't know. I just
said I was going to space

00:03:57.908 --> 00:04:00.453
and everyone on Twitter got very angry.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.207
Well, travel safe.

00:04:04.207 --> 00:04:06.102
Thank you.

00:04:06.102 --> 00:04:06.935
Thank you.

00:04:06.935 --> 00:04:11.279
You're the first person to
actually wish me safe travels.

00:04:11.279 --> 00:04:15.660
Everyone else just spray
painted my garage door.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.125
You know, do you want to come with me?

00:04:17.125 --> 00:04:18.400
Me?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.790
Yes. I was going to bring mittens,

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:20.870
but now I'd rather bring you.

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.490
I would love to go to space.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.410
Well let's go to space.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.243
Let's go to space.

00:04:24.243 --> 00:04:26.042
We have ice cream.
You're going to love it.

00:04:26.042 --> 00:04:26.878
Shotgun.

00:04:36.694 --> 00:04:39.051
I told you inflation was dangerous.

00:04:39.051 --> 00:04:42.603
Vodka Martini. Shaken, to-go.

